1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,013
Welcome to Unit Seven of Algebra One:
exponents and exponential functions.

2
00:00:05,463 --> 00:00:08,471
In this lesson, we'll learn the three main
exponent rules.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:14,140
An exponent counts repeated
multiplication. Two to the fourth means

4
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,664
two times two times two times two, which
is sixteen.

5
00:00:18,114 --> 00:00:20,845
The two is the base, and the four is the
exponent.

6
00:00:21,967 --> 00:00:26,596
Product rule: when you multiply powers
with the same base, add the exponents.

7
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:33,425
x squared times x cubed is x times x,
times x times x times x. That's x to the

8
00:00:33,425 --> 00:00:33,915
fifth.

9
00:00:35,033 --> 00:00:39,769
Quotient rule: when you divide powers with
the same base, subtract the exponents.

10
00:00:40,219 --> 00:00:45,147
x to the seventh over x squared is x to
the fifth, because two of the x's cancel.

11
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:50,405
Power rule: when you raise a power to a
power, multiply the exponents.

12
00:00:50,855 --> 00:00:55,378
x squared, all cubed, is x squared three
times, which is x to the sixth.

13
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,980
Now combine them. Simplify two x cubed,
times three x to the fourth.

14
00:01:01,430 --> 00:01:06,932
Multiply the numbers: two times three is
six. Add the exponents: x to the seventh.

15
00:01:06,932 --> 00:01:09,281
The answer is six x to the seventh.

16
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:15,328
Your turn. Simplify x to the fifth times x
cubed, all over x to the fourth.

17
00:01:15,778 --> 00:01:17,229
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:17,679 --> 00:01:22,529
The top is x to the eighth. Then eight
minus four is four. The answer is x to the

19
00:01:22,529 --> 00:01:22,948
fourth.

20
00:01:24,066 --> 00:01:28,183
Let's simplify an expression using several
exponent rules in a row.

21
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:35,350
Simplify: two x cubed y, all squared,
times three x y to the fourth, over six x

22
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:37,014
to the fifth y squared.

23
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:43,139
First the power of a product. Square each
factor: two squared is four, x cubed

24
00:01:43,139 --> 00:01:45,770
squared is x to the sixth, and y squared.

25
00:01:46,899 --> 00:01:52,578
Multiply by three x y to the fourth. Four
times three is twelve, and add exponents:

26
00:01:52,578 --> 00:01:54,835
x to the seventh, y to the sixth.

27
00:01:55,966 --> 00:01:58,654
Now divide by six x to the fifth y
squared.

28
00:01:59,799 --> 00:02:02,807
Twelve over six is two, and subtract
exponents.

29
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:06,279
That leaves two x squared y to the fourth.

30
00:02:07,399 --> 00:02:11,047
The expression simplifies to two x squared
y to the fourth.

31
00:02:12,166 --> 00:02:17,257
Watch out. When you raise a product to a
power, raise every factor, including the

32
00:02:17,257 --> 00:02:22,410
coefficient. Multiplying adds exponents,
dividing subtracts them, and a power of a

33
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:23,793
power multiplies them.

34
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:30,103
Your turn. Simplify three a squared b,
cubed, over nine a to the fourth b. Pause

35
00:02:30,103 --> 00:02:31,461
the video and try it.

36
00:02:35,999 --> 00:02:41,226
The top is twenty seven a to the sixth b
cubed. Divide: three a squared b squared.

37
00:02:42,366 --> 00:02:47,055
What could two to the zero, or two to the
negative three, possibly mean? In this

38
00:02:47,055 --> 00:02:48,403
lesson, we'll find out.

39
00:02:49,533 --> 00:02:53,903
Look at the pattern. Two cubed is eight,
two squared is four, two to the first is

40
00:02:53,903 --> 00:02:54,119
two.

41
00:02:54,569 --> 00:03:00,212
Each step down divides by two. So two to
the zero is one. In fact, any nonzero

42
00:03:00,212 --> 00:03:02,527
number to the zero power is one.

43
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:08,387
Keep going down the pattern. Two to the
negative one is one half, and two to the

44
00:03:08,387 --> 00:03:09,981
negative two is one fourth.

45
00:03:10,431 --> 00:03:15,853
A negative exponent means take the
reciprocal. x to the negative n equals one

46
00:03:15,853 --> 00:03:16,980
over x to the n.

47
00:03:18,099 --> 00:03:21,065
Five to the negative two is one over
twenty-five.

48
00:03:21,515 --> 00:03:26,895
And one over three to the negative two is
three squared, which is nine. A negative

49
00:03:26,895 --> 00:03:29,323
exponent in the denominator moves up.

50
00:03:30,466 --> 00:03:33,815
Simplify x to the negative three times x
to the fifth.

51
00:03:34,265 --> 00:03:38,489
Add the exponents: negative three plus
five is two. So it's x squared.

52
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:44,070
A common mistake: a negative exponent does
not make the number negative.

53
00:03:44,520 --> 00:03:47,784
Two to the negative one is one half, not
negative two.

54
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:53,178
Your turn. Simplify four to the negative
one, plus seven to the zero.

55
00:03:53,628 --> 00:03:55,079
Pause the video and try it.

56
00:03:55,529 --> 00:04:00,985
Four to the negative one is one fourth,
and seven to the zero is one. The total is

57
00:04:00,985 --> 00:04:02,249
one and one fourth.

58
00:04:02,366 --> 00:04:03,366
Next time, we'll look at fractional
exponents. If this helped, subscribe to

59
00:04:03,366 --> 00:04:07,206
Here's a worked example that clears zero
and negative exponents.

60
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:14,074
Simplify, using only positive exponents:
four a to the negative three b to the

61
00:04:14,074 --> 00:04:17,422
zero, over two a squared b to the negative
four.

62
00:04:18,566 --> 00:04:20,315
First, b to the zero is one.

63
00:04:21,433 --> 00:04:22,755
Four over two is two.

64
00:04:23,899 --> 00:04:28,571
For a, subtract exponents: negative three
minus two is negative five.

65
00:04:29,699 --> 00:04:34,497
A negative exponent in the denominator
moves to the numerator and becomes

66
00:04:34,497 --> 00:04:36,206
positive: b to the fourth.

67
00:04:37,333 --> 00:04:41,194
Finally, a to the negative five moves down
to become a to the fifth.

68
00:04:42,333 --> 00:04:45,319
The answer is two b to the fourth over a
to the fifth.

69
00:04:46,466 --> 00:04:51,291
Watch out. A negative exponent means take
the reciprocal, not make the number

70
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:56,179
negative. Only the factor with that
exponent moves, not the coefficient. And x

71
00:04:56,179 --> 00:04:59,501
to the zero is one, but three x to the
zero is three.

72
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:05,242
Your turn. Simplify three x to the
negative two, all to the negative two.

73
00:05:05,242 --> 00:05:06,947
Pause the video and try it.

74
00:05:11,466 --> 00:05:16,578
Multiply exponents: three to the negative
two times x to the fourth, which is x to

75
00:05:16,578 --> 00:05:17,887
the fourth over nine.

76
00:05:19,033 --> 00:05:23,948
Exponents don't have to be whole numbers.
In this lesson, we'll see what fractional

77
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:24,836
exponents mean.

78
00:05:25,966 --> 00:05:30,988
Nine to the one half, squared, is nine to
the first, which is nine. So nine to the

79
00:05:30,988 --> 00:05:34,478
one half must be the square root of nine,
which is three.

80
00:05:34,928 --> 00:05:38,107
In general, x to the one half is the
square root of x.

81
00:05:39,233 --> 00:05:43,902
The same idea works for cube roots. Eight
to the one third is the cube root of

82
00:05:43,902 --> 00:05:45,100
eight, which is two.

83
00:05:46,233 --> 00:05:51,566
In general, x to the m over n is the n-th
root of x, raised to the m.

84
00:05:52,016 --> 00:05:55,430
The bottom of the fraction is the root,
and the top is the power.

85
00:05:56,566 --> 00:05:58,337
Evaluate eight to the two thirds.

86
00:05:58,787 --> 00:06:03,054
The cube root of eight is two, and two
squared is four. So eight to the two

87
00:06:03,054 --> 00:06:03,907
thirds is four.

88
00:06:04,357 --> 00:06:06,661
Taking the root first keeps the numbers
small.

89
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:13,168
The exponent rules still apply. x to the
one half times x to the one half is x to

90
00:06:13,168 --> 00:06:14,626
the first, which is x.

91
00:06:15,766 --> 00:06:18,774
Your turn. Evaluate twenty-seven to the
two thirds.

92
00:06:19,224 --> 00:06:20,675
Pause the video and try it.

93
00:06:21,125 --> 00:06:24,688
The cube root of twenty-seven is three,
and three squared is nine.

94
00:06:25,833 --> 00:06:29,780
Let's evaluate rational exponents by
turning them into radicals.

95
00:06:31,200 --> 00:06:36,085
Evaluate twenty seven to the two thirds,
and sixteen to the negative three fourths.

96
00:06:37,233 --> 00:06:41,853
The denominator is the root and the
numerator is the power. So take the cube

97
00:06:41,853 --> 00:06:44,102
root of twenty seven, then square it.

98
00:06:45,233 --> 00:06:47,836
The cube root is three, and three squared
is nine.

99
00:06:48,966 --> 00:06:53,425
For the second, the negative means
reciprocal: one over sixteen to the three

100
00:06:53,425 --> 00:06:53,894
fourths.

101
00:06:55,033 --> 00:06:58,126
The fourth root of sixteen is two, and two
cubed is eight.

102
00:06:59,266 --> 00:07:02,488
So sixteen to the negative three fourths
is one eighth.

103
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:08,544
Twenty seven to the two thirds is nine,
and sixteen to the negative three fourths

104
00:07:08,544 --> 00:07:09,393
is one eighth.

105
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:16,055
Watch out. x to the m over n is the nth
root of x, to the m. Take the root first

106
00:07:16,055 --> 00:07:21,439
to keep the numbers small. And a negative
exponent gives a reciprocal, never a

107
00:07:21,439 --> 00:07:22,544
negative answer.

108
00:07:23,666 --> 00:07:28,317
Your turn. Evaluate thirty two to the
three fifths. Pause the video and try it.

109
00:07:32,866 --> 00:07:36,045
The fifth root of thirty two is two, and
two cubed is eight.

110
00:07:37,166 --> 00:07:42,528
Scientists write huge and tiny numbers
with powers of ten. In this lesson, we'll

111
00:07:42,528 --> 00:07:44,270
learn scientific notation.

112
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:49,410
A number in scientific notation looks like
a times ten to the n.

113
00:07:49,860 --> 00:07:53,935
The number a is at least one and less than
ten, and n is an integer.

114
00:07:55,066 --> 00:07:58,522
Write three hundred forty thousand in
scientific notation.

115
00:07:58,972 --> 00:08:04,155
Move the decimal point five places to the
left to get three point four. So it's

116
00:08:04,155 --> 00:08:06,780
three point four times ten to the fifth.

117
00:08:07,899 --> 00:08:11,206
Now write zero point zero zero zero six
two.

118
00:08:11,656 --> 00:08:16,958
Move the decimal four places to the right
to get six point two. Small numbers get

119
00:08:16,958 --> 00:08:21,213
negative exponents: six point two times
ten to the negative four.

120
00:08:22,333 --> 00:08:25,746
To multiply, multiply the numbers and add
the exponents.

121
00:08:26,196 --> 00:08:31,159
Three times ten to the fourth, times two
times ten to the fifth, is six times ten

122
00:08:31,159 --> 00:08:31,956
to the ninth.

123
00:08:33,099 --> 00:08:36,406
To divide, divide the numbers and subtract
the exponents.

124
00:08:36,856 --> 00:08:42,098
Eight times ten to the sixth, divided by
four times ten to the two, is two times

125
00:08:42,098 --> 00:08:43,277
ten to the fourth.

126
00:08:44,399 --> 00:08:50,254
Your turn. Multiply five times ten cubed
by four times ten to the sixth. Remember,

127
00:08:50,254 --> 00:08:53,253
the answer must be in scientific notation.

128
00:08:53,703 --> 00:08:55,153
Pause the video and try it.

129
00:08:55,603 --> 00:09:01,247
Five times four is twenty, and three plus
six is nine. Twenty times ten to the ninth

130
00:09:01,247 --> 00:09:03,262
is two times ten to the tenth.

131
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:09,264
Here's a worked example of multiplying and
dividing in scientific notation.

132
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:16,270
Light travels about three times ten to the
eighth meters per second. The Sun is about

133
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:21,578
one point five times ten to the eleventh
meters away. How long does sunlight take

134
00:09:21,578 --> 00:09:22,561
to reach Earth?

135
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:26,132
Time equals distance divided by rate.

136
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:31,384
Divide the numbers: one point five over
three is zero point five.

137
00:09:32,533 --> 00:09:36,501
Divide the powers: ten to the eleven minus
eight, which is ten cubed.

138
00:09:37,633 --> 00:09:42,817
Zero point five is less than one, so shift
the decimal: five times ten squared.

139
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:46,889
That's five hundred seconds, a little over
eight minutes.

140
00:09:48,033 --> 00:09:52,253
Sunlight takes about five times ten
squared seconds, which is about eight

141
00:09:52,253 --> 00:09:53,409
point three minutes.

142
00:09:54,533 --> 00:09:59,213
Watch out. Group the numbers together and
the powers of ten together. The front

143
00:09:59,213 --> 00:10:04,188
number must be at least one and less than
ten. And moving the decimal one place left

144
00:10:04,188 --> 00:10:05,669
adds one to the exponent.

145
00:10:06,800 --> 00:10:12,131
Your turn. Multiply four times ten to the
fifth by six times ten cubed, in

146
00:10:12,131 --> 00:10:15,589
scientific notation. Pause the video and
try it.

147
00:10:20,133 --> 00:10:25,527
Four times six is twenty four, and ten to
the eighth. Adjust to two point four times

148
00:10:25,527 --> 00:10:26,619
ten to the ninth.

149
00:10:27,766 --> 00:10:32,299
In this lesson, we'll meet exponential
functions, where the variable is in the

150
00:10:32,299 --> 00:10:32,822
exponent.

151
00:10:33,966 --> 00:10:38,830
An exponential function has the form f of
x equals a times b to the x.

152
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:43,888
a is the starting value, and b is the
base, a positive number that isn't one.

153
00:10:45,033 --> 00:10:47,955
Make a table for f of x equals two to the
x.

154
00:10:48,405 --> 00:10:54,101
At x equals zero, the value is one. Then
two, four, eight. Each step multiplies by

155
00:10:54,101 --> 00:10:54,379
two.

156
00:10:55,499 --> 00:11:00,398
Plot the points and connect them. The
curve rises slowly at first, then faster

157
00:11:00,398 --> 00:11:01,089
and faster.

158
00:11:01,539 --> 00:11:05,549
On the left, it gets close to zero but
never touches the x axis.

159
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:12,618
Take f of x equals three times two to the
x. At x equals zero, f equals three.

160
00:11:13,068 --> 00:11:16,460
So a is the y intercept: the value where
the graph starts.

161
00:11:17,599 --> 00:11:19,882
Here's the key difference from linear
functions.

162
00:11:20,332 --> 00:11:25,073
A linear function adds the same amount
each step. An exponential function

163
00:11:25,073 --> 00:11:27,671
multiplies by the same factor each step.

164
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:34,546
Your turn. For f of x equals five times
three to the x, find f of zero and f of

165
00:11:34,546 --> 00:11:34,837
two.

166
00:11:35,287 --> 00:11:36,737
Pause the video and try it.

167
00:11:37,187 --> 00:11:41,923
f of zero is five. f of two is five times
nine, which is forty-five.

168
00:11:43,066 --> 00:11:46,458
Let's write an exponential function from a
table and graph it.

169
00:11:48,166 --> 00:11:54,093
Write y equals a times b to the x for this
table: x zero, one, two, three gives y

170
00:11:54,093 --> 00:11:57,019
five, ten, twenty, forty. Then graph it.

171
00:11:58,166 --> 00:12:02,731
First check the differences: five, then
ten. Not constant, so it's not linear.

172
00:12:03,866 --> 00:12:09,494
Check the ratios: each is two. A constant
ratio means exponential, with b equals

173
00:12:09,494 --> 00:12:09,775
two.

174
00:12:10,899 --> 00:12:15,230
The value at x equals zero is the initial
value, a equals five.

175
00:12:16,366 --> 00:12:18,798
So y equals five times two to the x.

176
00:12:19,933 --> 00:12:25,490
The function is y equals five times two to
the x. It starts at five and doubles each

177
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:25,821
step.

178
00:12:26,966 --> 00:12:31,754
Watch out. A constant difference means
linear, and a constant ratio means

179
00:12:31,754 --> 00:12:37,132
exponential. a is the y value when x is
zero. And b greater than one means growth,

180
00:12:37,132 --> 00:12:39,297
between zero and one means decay.

181
00:12:40,433 --> 00:12:45,404
Your turn. x zero, one, two gives y eighty
one, twenty seven, nine. Write the

182
00:12:45,404 --> 00:12:47,793
function. Pause the video and try it.

183
00:12:52,333 --> 00:12:58,133
Each ratio is one third, and the start is
eighty one. y equals eighty one times one

184
00:12:58,133 --> 00:12:59,181
third to the x.

185
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:05,178
Exponential functions model things that
grow or shrink by a percent. In this

186
00:13:05,178 --> 00:13:07,681
lesson, we'll look at growth and decay.

187
00:13:08,800 --> 00:13:11,808
When the base b is greater than one, the
function grows.

188
00:13:12,258 --> 00:13:17,444
A population of one hundred that doubles
each year is one hundred times two to the

189
00:13:17,444 --> 00:13:17,570
t.

190
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:21,921
When b is between zero and one, the
function decays.

191
00:13:22,371 --> 00:13:27,406
A forty milligram dose that halves every
hour is forty times one half to the t.

192
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:31,989
For growth by a percent r, use b equals
one plus r.

193
00:13:32,439 --> 00:13:38,011
A two thousand dollar investment growing
five percent a year is two thousand times

194
00:13:38,011 --> 00:13:43,311
one point zero five to the t. After two
years, that's two thousand two hundred

195
00:13:43,311 --> 00:13:44,194
five dollars.

196
00:13:45,333 --> 00:13:48,960
For decay by a percent r, use b equals one
minus r.

197
00:13:49,410 --> 00:13:53,954
A twenty thousand dollar car losing
fifteen percent each year is twenty

198
00:13:53,954 --> 00:13:56,898
thousand times zero point eight five to
the t.

199
00:13:58,033 --> 00:14:00,401
To decide growth or decay, look at the
base.

200
00:14:00,851 --> 00:14:06,504
One point zero three is greater than one:
growth of three percent. Zero point nine

201
00:14:06,504 --> 00:14:09,193
is less than one: decay of ten percent.

202
00:14:10,333 --> 00:14:15,402
Your turn. A town of eight thousand grows
four percent per year. Write the model,

203
00:14:15,402 --> 00:14:17,843
and find the population after one year.

204
00:14:18,293 --> 00:14:19,743
Pause the video and try it.

205
00:14:20,193 --> 00:14:25,374
The model is eight thousand times one
point zero four to the t. After one year,

206
00:14:25,374 --> 00:14:28,193
that's eight thousand three hundred
twenty.

207
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:33,237
Here's a worked example of exponential
decay with a real price.

208
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:39,855
A car costs twenty four thousand dollars
and loses fifteen percent of its value

209
00:14:39,855 --> 00:14:43,861
each year. Write a model and find its
value after four years.

210
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:48,669
Decay uses y equals a times one minus r,
to the t.

211
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:54,704
The starting value a is twenty four
thousand, and r is fifteen percent, or

212
00:14:54,704 --> 00:14:56,029
zero point one five.

213
00:14:57,166 --> 00:15:02,692
The decay factor is one minus zero point
one five, which is zero point eight five.

214
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:08,206
Zero point eight five to the fourth is
about zero point five two two.

215
00:15:09,333 --> 00:15:14,303
Multiply by twenty four thousand: about
twelve thousand five hundred twenty eight

216
00:15:14,303 --> 00:15:14,794
dollars.

217
00:15:15,933 --> 00:15:21,237
The model is y equals twenty four thousand
times zero point eight five to the t.

218
00:15:21,237 --> 00:15:26,408
After four years, the car is worth about
twelve thousand five hundred dollars.

219
00:15:27,533 --> 00:15:32,601
Watch out. Growth uses one plus r, decay
uses one minus r. Convert percents to

220
00:15:32,601 --> 00:15:37,603
decimals. And losing fifteen percent a
year for four years is not the same as

221
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:41,826
losing sixty percent, because each loss is
from a smaller amount.

222
00:15:42,966 --> 00:15:48,317
Your turn. A town of eight thousand people
grows three percent per year. What is the

223
00:15:48,317 --> 00:15:51,884
population after five years? Pause the
video and try it.

224
00:15:56,433 --> 00:16:01,583
Eight thousand times one point zero three
to the fifth is about nine thousand two

225
00:16:01,583 --> 00:16:02,918
hundred seventy four.

226
00:16:04,066 --> 00:16:09,543
In Unit Four we saw arithmetic sequences,
which add the same number each time. In

227
00:16:09,543 --> 00:16:14,818
this last lesson of Unit Seven, we'll see
geometric sequences, which multiply.

228
00:16:15,966 --> 00:16:20,083
In three, six, twelve, twenty-four, each
term is twice the one before.

229
00:16:20,533 --> 00:16:25,483
The constant multiplier is called the
common ratio, r. Here r equals two.

230
00:16:26,633 --> 00:16:32,931
The formula for the n-th term is a sub n
equals a sub one times r to the n minus

231
00:16:32,931 --> 00:16:33,246
one.

232
00:16:33,696 --> 00:16:37,920
For our sequence, a sub n equals three
times two to the n minus one.

233
00:16:39,066 --> 00:16:40,346
Find the seventh term.

234
00:16:40,796 --> 00:16:45,362
Three times two to the sixth is three
times sixty-four, which is one hundred

235
00:16:45,362 --> 00:16:46,023
ninety-two.

236
00:16:47,166 --> 00:16:51,625
Compare. Two, five, eight, eleven adds
three each time, so it's arithmetic.

237
00:16:52,075 --> 00:16:57,863
Two, six, eighteen, fifty-four multiplies
by three each time, so it's geometric. A

238
00:16:57,863 --> 00:17:02,592
geometric sequence is an exponential
function on the whole numbers.

239
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:09,186
The ratio can be a fraction. In eighty,
forty, twenty, ten, the ratio is one half,

240
00:17:09,186 --> 00:17:10,517
so the terms shrink.

241
00:17:11,666 --> 00:17:16,061
Your turn. Find the sixth term of five,
fifteen, forty-five, and so on.

242
00:17:16,511 --> 00:17:17,961
Pause the video and try it.

243
00:17:18,411 --> 00:17:23,113
The ratio is three. Five times three to
the fifth is five times two hundred

244
00:17:23,113 --> 00:17:26,561
forty-three, which is one thousand two
hundred fifteen.

245
00:17:27,700 --> 00:17:31,711
Let's write the rule for a geometric
sequence and find a later term.

246
00:17:33,133 --> 00:17:37,980
For the sequence three, negative six,
twelve, negative twenty four, and so on,

247
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:40,963
write an explicit rule and find the eighth
term.

248
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:46,495
The common ratio is negative six over
three, which is negative two.

249
00:17:47,633 --> 00:17:48,892
The first term is three.

250
00:17:50,033 --> 00:17:55,580
The explicit rule is a sub n equals three
times negative two to the n minus one.

251
00:17:56,700 --> 00:17:58,855
For the eighth term, the exponent is
seven.

252
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:05,149
Negative two to the seventh is negative
one twenty eight. Times three is negative

253
00:18:05,149 --> 00:18:06,293
three eighty four.

254
00:18:07,433 --> 00:18:12,223
The rule is three times negative two to
the n minus one, and the eighth term is

255
00:18:12,223 --> 00:18:14,345
negative three hundred eighty four.

256
00:18:15,467 --> 00:18:21,173
Watch out. The exponent is n minus one,
not n. Put a negative ratio in parentheses

257
00:18:21,173 --> 00:18:26,810
so the sign is raised too. And remember
arithmetic sequences add a constant while

258
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:28,480
geometric ones multiply.

259
00:18:29,600 --> 00:18:34,808
Your turn. Find the sixth term of one
sixty, eighty, forty, and so on. Pause the

260
00:18:34,808 --> 00:18:35,915
video and try it.

261
00:18:40,433 --> 00:18:44,977
The ratio is one half. One sixty times one
half to the fifth is five.

262
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:50,766
Let's finish Unit Seven by comparing
linear and exponential growth with real

263
00:18:50,766 --> 00:18:51,135
money.

264
00:18:52,567 --> 00:18:57,404
Plan A starts with one thousand dollars
and adds one hundred per year. Plan B

265
00:18:57,404 --> 00:19:02,367
starts with one thousand and earns six
percent per year. Write both models, and

266
00:19:02,367 --> 00:19:06,263
decide which is ahead after five years and
after twenty years.

267
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:12,200
Plan A adds a constant amount, so it's
linear: one thousand plus one hundred t.

268
00:19:13,333 --> 00:19:18,717
Plan B grows by a constant percent, so
it's exponential: one thousand times one

269
00:19:18,717 --> 00:19:20,352
point zero six to the t.

270
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:24,103
After five years, A has fifteen hundred
dollars.

271
00:19:25,233 --> 00:19:28,263
B has about thirteen hundred thirty eight.
A is ahead.

272
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,597
After twenty years, A has three thousand.

273
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:36,232
B has about thirty two hundred seven. Now
B is ahead.

274
00:19:37,367 --> 00:19:43,041
Plan A is ahead after five years, but plan
B overtakes it and is ahead after twenty.

275
00:19:43,041 --> 00:19:45,879
Exponential growth always wins eventually.

276
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:52,433
Watch out. A constant amount means linear,
a constant percent means exponential. In

277
00:19:52,433 --> 00:19:57,735
the short term, the linear plan can be
ahead. In the long run, exponential growth

278
00:19:57,735 --> 00:19:58,520
always wins.

279
00:19:59,667 --> 00:20:04,832
Your turn. Plan C starts with one thousand
and earns ten percent per year. What's it

280
00:20:04,832 --> 00:20:09,629
worth after five years, and is it ahead of
plan A? Pause the video and try it.

281
00:20:14,167 --> 00:20:19,123
One thousand times one point one to the
fifth is about sixteen hundred eleven.

282
00:20:19,123 --> 00:20:22,999
That's more than fifteen hundred, so yes,
it's already ahead.

283
